{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-kvrk-uor3-g5fo-plme","published":"2026-11-13T17:02:28Z","modified":"2026-11-24T21:15:30.315153617Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-114133"],"summary":"Nuxt is an open-source web development framework for Vue.js. From 3.13.0 until 4.6.2, the server-island renderer…","details":"Nuxt is an open-source web development framework for Vue.js. From 3.13.0 until 4.6.2, the server-island renderer serializes raw useHeadSafe entry input into the island response without preserving the safe-input marker, and NuxtIsland later inserts that input into the page head as an ordinary entry. An application that passes attacker-controlled data to useHeadSafe in a .server.vue component or page, or in a component rendered through NuxtIsland, can therefore render values normally removed by the allowlist, including event-handler attributes or executable script content, resulting in stored cross-site scripting in the application origin. This issue is fixed in version 4.6.2 .","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kyverno-policy-reporter-ui-dev","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.23","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/kyverno-policy-reporter-ui-dev"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"2.6.1-r0"}]}],"versions":["2.6.1-r0","2.7.0-r0","2.7.0-r1","2.7.0-r2","2.7.1-r0","2.7.1-r1","2.7.1-r2","2.7.2-r0","2.7.2-r1","2.7.3-r0","2.8.1-r0","2.8.1-r1","2.8.1-r2","2.8.1-r3","2.8.1-r4","2.8.1-r5","2.9.0-r1","2.9.1-r0","2.9.1-r1","2.9.1-r2","2.9.1-r3","2.9.1-r4","2.9.1-r5","2.9.1-r6"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-kvrk-uor3-g5fo-plme.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kyverno-policy-reporter-ui-dev","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/kyverno-policy-reporter-ui-dev"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"2.6.1-r0"}]}],"versions":["2.6.1-r0","2.7.0-r0","2.7.0-r1","2.7.0-r2","2.7.1-r0","2.7.1-r1","2.7.1-r2","2.7.2-r0","2.7.2-r1","2.7.3